config MCUHOME_RTT_REINIT
	bool "Re-initialize the RTT control block at boot"
	depends on USE_SEGGER_RTT
	default y if LOG_BACKEND_RTT
	help
	  Log-only RTT builds never re-initialize the RTT control block: the
	  log backend writes through the NoLock API, which skips SEGGER's lazy
	  init. After a reset the block keeps stale read/write offsets from
	  the previous session — the buffer can appear permanently full,
	  wedging the log thread and silencing all output. This adds a
	  PRE_KERNEL_1 SYS_INIT hook that calls SEGGER_RTT_Init() explicitly,
	  before the log core starts (upstream candidate Z7).
